    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After more than two years of regulatory proceedings under the EU's competition law, Brussels has finally rejected the tech giant's attempts to make things right. Now, a formal decision on a major financial sanction is expected soon, before the summer break, with a penalty reaching into the hundreds of millions. This is just the latest fine for the parent company with a long record of such punishments, all for putting its own interests ahead of fair competition by favoring its own services in search rankings, hurting the smaller companies getting squeezed out.",
