    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The rule enforcers in the political union are finalizing a substantial fine against a major tech company for self-preferencing in search results. The proposed fixes from the company were deemed insufficient, and the lengthy regulatory proceedings have led to a multi-hundred-million-euro penalty. This adds another recurring regulatory penalty to the corporate parent's record, a financial penalty designed to ensure the playing field remains level for all competing businesses.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
